{"name":"Bungalow Maple","hex":"#e4c590","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bungalow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single-storey house, typically with rooms all on one level, or sometimes also with upper rooms set into the roof space.","A thatched or tiled one-story house in India surrounded by a wide veranda; a similar house in this style."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bungalow"},{"term":"maple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of any species of genus Acer, characterized by (usually) palmate, five-lobed leaves and winged seeds, and often grown for syrup or wood","A small tree (Acer campestre), known as the common maple, field maple, or hedge maple, which has palmate leaves with five lobes and winged seeds, and is chiefly native to East Asia, Europe, North Africa, and North America."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the light-brown colour of the wood of a maple tree (etymology 1, noun sense 3).","Of the flavour of, or made with, maple syrup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bungalow","blocks":[{"text":"A bungalow is a small house or cottage that is typically single- or one-and-a-half-storey. If a smaller upper storey exists, then it is frequently set in the roof and windows that come out from the roof. It may be surrounded by wide verandas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/149MyrtleReedsburgWI.JPG/330px-149MyrtleReedsburgWI.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bungalow","wikidata":"Q850107"},{"title":"Maple","blocks":[{"text":"Acer is a genus of trees and shrubs commonly known as maples. The genus is placed in the soapberry family Sapindaceae. There are approximately 132 species, most of which are native to East Asia, with a number also appearing in Europe, northern Africa, and North America. Only one species, Acer laurinum, extends to the Southern Hemisphere. The type species of the genus is the sycamore maple Acer pseudoplatanus, one of the most common maple species in Europe. Most maples have easily identifiable palmate leaves and all share distinctive winged fruits. The closest relative of the maples is the small east Asian genus Dipteronia, followed by the more widespread genus Aesculus. Maple syrup is made from the sap of some maple species. It is one of the most common genera of trees in Asia. Many maple species are grown in gardens where they are valued for their autumn colour and often decorative foliage, some also for their attractive flowers, fruit, or bark."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Acer_pseudoplatanus_002.jpg/330px-Acer_pseudoplatanus_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maple","wikidata":"Q42292"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/StateLibQld_2_228966_Home_Building_Publishing_Company_home%2C_Design_No._3%2C_1939.jpg/500px-StateLibQld_2_228966_Home_Building_Publishing_Company_home%2C_Design_No._3%2C_1939.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/StateLibQld_2_228966_Home_Building_Publishing_Company_home%2C_Design_No._3%2C_1939.jpg/500px-StateLibQld_2_228966_Home_Building_Publishing_Company_home%2C_Design_No._3%2C_1939.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elevation and floor plan of an Australian bungalow-style residence, 1939.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStateLibQld_2_228966_Home_Building_Publishing_Company_home%2C_Design_No._3%2C_1939.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/100_Bungalows_of_Architectural_Distinction_-_DPLA_-_45a4746debb1bb15282e0547198ab930_%28page_56%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-100_Bungalows_of_